! DBG89S.DBG - SET SCOPE at the program's start and after its end (README.md).
! VMS's log leaves out a command that fails, so a comment names each case first.
SHOW CALLS
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE 1 at START: the frame below the main routine
SET SCOPE 1
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE PC
EXAMINE/INSTRUCTION .PC
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1 at START
CANCEL SCOPE
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 2 at START
CANCEL SCOPE
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 2
SHOW SCOPE
CANCEL SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE REC, not active yet
SET SCOPE REC
SHOW SCOPE
!> EXAMINE R2 under SET SCOPE REC, not active
EXAMINE R2
!> EXAMINE Y under SET SCOPE REC
EXAMINE Y
!> EXAMINE DEPTH under SET SCOPE REC
EXAMINE DEPTH
CANCEL SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE 0
SET SCOPE 0
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE 0, kept across a break in another routine?
SET BREAK DBG89B
GO
SHOW CALLS
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
CANCEL SCOPE
CANCEL BREAK/ALL
!> GO to the end
GO
!> After the end: SHOW SCOPE
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE 1
SET SCOPE 1
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 0
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 0
!> SET SCOPE DBG89\REC
SET SCOPE DBG89\REC
SHOW SCOPE
!> EXAMINE Y
EXAMINE Y
!> CANCEL SCOPE
CANCEL SCOPE
SHOW SCOPE
